meta {
  name: Space Create Space
  type: http
  seq: 169
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/xrpc/com.atproto.space.createSpace
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "spaceType": "org.example.bucket",
    "skey": "main",
    "policy": {
      "$type": "com.atproto.memberspace.policy",
      "publicRead": false,
      "publicWrite": false,
      "publishPolicy": false,
      "publishMembers": false
    }
  }
}

docs {
  Atproto Spaces: create a space with the authenticated account as its authority. The URI is
  at://{callerDid}/space/{spaceType}/{skey}; "skey" is optional (a TID is generated when
  absent) and uses record-key syntax.

  "policy" is an open union over the three baseline policies, all implemented here:
  com.atproto.personalspace.policy (the authority alone), com.atproto.memberspace.policy
  (publicRead, publicWrite, optional allowedApps — absent admits any app, [] none — and the
  publishPolicy/publishMembers flags), and com.atproto.managedspace.policy (managingApp, a
  did#serviceId reference asked through checkAccess, and publishPolicy). The policy is stored
  normalized: unknown fields dropped, defaults filled. An unknown $type is refused with 400
  UnsupportedPolicy and never stored. With publishPolicy, a com.atproto.space.policy/self record
  lands in the authority's repo in the same commit.

  Responds { space }. Errors: 400 SpaceAlreadyExists when an active space already holds the
  URI (a deleted one may be created again), 403 InsufficientScope when the OAuth grant carries
  no "space:…?manage=create" covering the space.
}
